### 2. Test Objectives

The objective of this test strategy is to define the approach for testing the Vivi.lv website and to validate its functionality and usability.
The testing objectives are to:
* Verify that the system functions according to the defined requirements.
* Validate the main user journeys.
* Identify functional defects and usability issues.
* Verify a consistent user experience across the website.


### 3. Test Scope

In Scope

The following areas are included in the scope of testing:
* Public website pages
* Navigation
* Language selection
* Notifications
* News and news search
* Route changes
* Interactive map
* Train search
* Ticket selection
* Ticket purchase
* User authentication
* My Account
* Payment cards
* Favourite routes
* Purchase history
* Contact and support
* Accessibility
* Click-to-Call

Out of Scope

The following areas are excluded from the scope of testing:
* Backend services and internal system logic
* Database functionality
* Infrastructure and server performance testing
* Third-party service implementations
* Production infrastructure, monitoring, and system administration

### 4. Testing Approach

Testing will be performed using a black-box approach based on publicly available website functionality and defined user flows.

The following testing techniques will be used:

* Requirement-based testing to verify compliance with functional requirements.
* Scenario-based testing to validate end-to-end user journeys.
* Exploratory testing to identify unexpected behaviour and usability issues.
* Regression testing to verify that existing functionality continues to work after changes.


### 5. Test Types

Functional Testing
Functional testing will verify that system features operate according to the defined requirements.
Examples:
* Train search
* Ticket purchase
* User account management
* News search
* Contact form submission

Usability Testing
Usability testing will evaluate:
* Navigation clarity
* User interface consistency
* User interaction flow
* Error message clarity

Accessibility Testing
Accessibility testing will verify:
* Text size adjustment
* Colour contrast options
* Accessibility settings reset functionality

Regression Testing
Regression testing will confirm that existing functionality remains unaffected after changes or fixes.

### 6. Test Levels

System Testing
The website will be tested as a complete system from an end-user perspective.

Integration Testing
Available user-facing integrations will be validated where possible, including:
* Authentication flow
* Payment-related user flows
* External map functionality
* Email communication features

### 7. Test Environment

Testing will be performed using:

Environment:
* Web browser-based testing environment

Browsers:
* Google Chrome

Devices:
* Desktop computer

Testing Tools:
* Browser Developer Tools
* Jira defect tracking tool
* GitHub for documentation management

### 8. Test Data

Testing will use representative test data, including:

* Valid and invalid station selections
* Different travel dates
* Search criteria variations
* User account data
* Contact form input data
* Different accessibility settings

### 9. Entry Criteria

Testing can begin when:
* Requirements analysis has been completed.
* The test strategy has been approved.
* Test scenarios have been prepared.
* The test environment is available.
* The website is available for testing.

### 10. Exit Criteria

Testing can be completed when:
* Planned test scenarios have been executed.
* Critical user flows have been validated.
* Critical defects have been documented.
* Test results have been recorded.
* A test summary report has been completed.

11. Defect Management

Defects identified during testing shall be documented and tracked until resolution.

Each defect report shall include:

* Defect ID
* Summary
* Steps to reproduce
* Expected result
* Actual result
* Severity
* Priority
* Supporting evidence (if applicable)

### 12. Test Deliverables

The following testing documents will be produced:

* Test Checklists
* Test Scenarios
* Test Cases
* Test Execution Results
* Bug Reports
* Test Summary Report

13. Risks and Mitigation

Risk	Mitigation
Website functionality may change during testing. Update test documentation and test cases as needed.
Limited access to test accounts or test data may restrict test coverage.	 Perform testing using available accounts and document any limitations.
Third-party services may be unavailable or behave unexpectedly.	Verify user-facing functionality and document any third-party limitations.
